{"id":"l2-04-t1","title":"LLD interview tips: method and scoring","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: clarifying requirements, the timed method, naming, extensibility talk and what interviewers score. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"what-an-lld-interview-really-tests","title":"What an LLD interview really tests","html":"<p><strong>A low-level design (LLD) interview asks you to design classes and their relationships for a small system (parking lot, elevator, LRU cache, splitwise) in about 45 to 60 minutes.</strong> It is not about drawing perfect UML. It tests whether you can turn a vague idea into clean, extensible, working code under time pressure.</p>\n<p>What the interviewer scores, roughly:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Did you clarify requirements before coding?</li>\n<li>Are the entities and responsibilities sensible (SOLID)?</li>\n<li>Is it extensible when the next requirement arrives?</li>\n<li>Is the code correct, readable and runnable?</li>\n<li>Did you handle edge cases and concurrency?</li>\n<li>Did you communicate your trade-offs?</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 877.6 68\" width=\"877.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The shape of a good LLD interview\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M421.6 34 L477.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M421.6 34 L477.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M567.6 34 L623.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M567.6 34 L623.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M719.6 34 L775.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M719.6 34 L775.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Clarify</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Entities</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Class diagram</text><rect x=\"477.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"522.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Code core</text><rect x=\"623.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"671.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Edge cases</text><rect x=\"775.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"820.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Extend</text></svg><figcaption>The shape of a good LLD interview</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> \"Design a parking lot.\" A weak answer starts typing <code>class ParkingLot</code> at minute 1. A strong answer spends 5 minutes on scope (levels? vehicle types? pricing? entry/exit gates?), 5 on entities, 10 on a class sketch, 20 on core code, 10 on extensions.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Interview loops at Amazon (LLD with Leadership Principles), Uber, Flipkart, Swiggy and Atlassian commonly use machine-coding or LLD rounds; machine-coding rounds ask for runnable code in 90 to 120 minutes with tests.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> An architect asks the client questions before drawing walls.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Treating it as a pattern quiz; patterns are tools, not the goal.</li>\n<li>Silence: the interviewer cannot score what you do not say.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"clarifying-requirements","title":"Clarifying requirements","html":"<p><strong>Spend the first 5 to 8 minutes asking questions and writing the answers down.</strong> Ambiguity is deliberate; the interviewer wants to see you cut scope.</p>\n<p>Question buckets:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Actors:</strong> who uses it (customer, admin, guard)?</li>\n<li><strong>Core use cases:</strong> the 3 to 5 things it must do (park, unpark, find a free spot, pay).</li>\n<li><strong>Scale and shape:</strong> one lot or many? 100 or 100,000 spots? One process or distributed? (LLD is normally single process.)</li>\n<li><strong>Rules:</strong> pricing, limits, priorities, failures (full lot?).</li>\n<li><strong>Out of scope:</strong> payments gateway, UI, persistence. State them so you do not build them.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then write a short list on the board:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Functional:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  1. Park a vehicle -> returns ticket</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  2. Unpark with ticket -> returns fee</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  3. Show free spots per type</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Non-functional:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  - Thread-safe parking (many gates)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  - Easy to add new vehicle types and pricing rules</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Out of scope: payment gateway, UI, DB</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 670.8 68\" width=\"670.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Questions turn into a scoped list\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M268.4 34 L324.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M268.4 34 L324.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M492.4 34 L548.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M492.4 34 L548.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Vague prompt</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"223.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Questions</text><rect x=\"324.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"168\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"408.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Written requirements</text><rect x=\"548.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"603.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Agreed scope</text></svg><figcaption>Questions turn into a scoped list</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Asking \"single lot, 3 levels, 200 spots per level, cars/bikes/trucks, hourly pricing, multiple gates\" fixes the model: 600 spots, 3 spot sizes, pricing strategy, concurrency at the gates. Without it you might build a multi-city system or a single-spot toy.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Amazon bar-raisers explicitly watch whether you \"dive deep\" only after defining the problem; Google's design interviews grade \"handling ambiguity\".</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A tailor measures before cutting cloth.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Asking 30 questions; ask the 6 that change the design.</li>\n<li>Not confirming the list back (\"so we agree on these 4 use cases?\").</li>\n<li>Starting to code before the interviewer says go.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"the-method-with-a-clock","title":"The method with a clock","html":"<p><strong>Use a fixed script so you never freeze.</strong> Typical 45-minute budget:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Minutes</th>\n<th>Step</th>\n<th>Output</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>0 to 5</td>\n<td>Clarify</td>\n<td>Requirements list, out-of-scope list</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5 to 10</td>\n<td>Entities and relationships</td>\n<td>Nouns become classes, verbs become methods</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10 to 18</td>\n<td>Class diagram + patterns</td>\n<td>Interfaces, key relationships, where it varies</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>18 to 35</td>\n<td>Code the core flow</td>\n<td>Compiles; main flow works</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>35 to 42</td>\n<td>Edge cases, concurrency, tests</td>\n<td>Named failure modes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>42 to 45</td>\n<td>Extensions and wrap-up</td>\n<td>\"To add X, I change only Y\"</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>How to find entities: underline the nouns in the requirements (Vehicle, Spot, Ticket, Level), then ask who owns each action. Verbs (\"park\", \"calculate fee\") become methods on the entity that has the data.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Requirement noun/verb        ->   Design</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Vehicle, Spot, Ticket, Level ->   classes</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>park(vehicle)                ->   ParkingLot.park</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>fee(ticket)                  ->   PricingStrategy.fee</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>vehicle type varies          ->   enum + strategy / subclass</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 931.5999999999999 68\" width=\"931.5999999999999\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The clock keeps you moving\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M281.6 34 L337.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M281.6 34 L337.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M440.8 34 L496.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M440.8 34 L496.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M586.8 34 L642.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M586.8 34 L642.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M767.5999999999999 34 L823.5999999999999 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M767.5999999999999 34 L823.5999999999999 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Clarify (5)</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"226.39999999999998\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Entities (5)</text><rect x=\"337.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"389.20000000000005\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Diagram (8)</text><rect x=\"496.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"541.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Code (17)</text><rect x=\"642.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"705.1999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Edge cases (7)</text><rect x=\"823.5999999999999\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"871.5999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Extend (3)</text></svg><figcaption>The clock keeps you moving</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> At minute 18 you must be typing code. If you are still polishing the diagram, cut it: an interviewer prefers a working simple core over a perfect diagram with no code.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Machine-coding rounds at Flipkart/Swiggy/Razorpay grade \"working code, running demo, extensibility\" in a fixed time, in that order.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A chess clock: the position matters, but you must move.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Spending 20 minutes on UML.</li>\n<li>Coding everything before the core flow runs end to end.</li>\n<li>Skipping the last 3 minutes; the extension discussion often decides the hire/no-hire.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"naming-and-class-design","title":"Naming and class design","html":"<p><strong>Names carry your design.</strong> A good name lets the interviewer read your code without you explaining it.</p>\n<p>Rules:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Classes are nouns</strong> (<code>ParkingSpot</code>, <code>PricingStrategy</code>), <strong>methods are verbs</strong> (<code>park</code>, <code>calculateFee</code>), booleans read as questions (<code>isFree</code>).</li>\n<li>Name by role, not by type: <code>FeeCalculator</code>, not <code>Manager</code>/<code>Helper</code>/<code>Util</code>/<code>Data</code>.</li>\n<li>One class, one reason to change (Single Responsibility). If you need \"and\" to describe it, split it.</li>\n<li>Prefer small interfaces named after the capability (<code>Payable</code>, <code>Notifier</code>).</li>\n<li>Make fields <code>private final</code> unless mutation is the point; expose behavior, not data (tell, do not ask).</li>\n<li>Use enums for closed sets (<code>VehicleType</code>), strategies for open behavior.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// BEFORE: vague</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">class</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> Manager</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">void</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> doIt</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\"> t</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\"> x</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) { ... } }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// AFTER: intent clear</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">class</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> FeeCalculator</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    Money </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">calculate</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(Duration </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">parked</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, VehicleType </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">type</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) { ... }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Kotlin variant: <code>data class Ticket(val id: String, val spot: Spot, val entry: Instant)</code>; <code>sealed interface</code> for closed hierarchies.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 585.6 68\" width=\"585.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Good names make the structure obvious\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M254 34 L310 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M254 34 L310 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M400 34 L456 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M400 34 L456 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Vehicle</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ParkingLot</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Ticket</text><rect x=\"456\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"514.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">FeeCalculator</text></svg><figcaption>Good names make the structure obvious</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> <code>Level</code> holds its spots and finds a free one (<code>Optional&#x3C;Spot> findFree(VehicleType)</code>); <code>ParkingLot</code> only picks a level. Each class is 30 to 60 lines, understandable at a glance.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> The JDK is a good teacher: <code>Comparator</code>, <code>Executor</code>, <code>Supplier</code>, <code>List</code> are role names; Google Java Style and Effective Java Chapter 4 on class design.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Labels on kitchen jars: you never open the wrong one.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Utils</code> and <code>Manager</code> classes that become dumping grounds.</li>\n<li>Public mutable fields.</li>\n<li>Names like <code>data</code>, <code>temp</code>, <code>obj</code> in front of an interviewer.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"extensibility-talk","title":"Extensibility talk","html":"<p><strong>Interviewers always ask \"what if we add X?\". Prepare to answer with: which class changes, which does not.</strong> The goal is Open/Closed: extend by adding code, not editing working code.</p>\n<p>Pattern for the answer: \"Today X is an <code>enum</code> with a switch in one place. If a new type arrives I add a class implementing <code>Y</code> and register it; nothing else changes.\"</p>\n<p>Typical extensions and where to put the seam:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>New requirement</th>\n<th>Seam you prepared</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>New vehicle type</td>\n<td><code>VehicleType</code> enum + <code>SpotSize</code> mapping, or a Vehicle subclass</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New pricing rule (weekend, surge)</td>\n<td><code>PricingStrategy</code> interface</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New payment method</td>\n<td><code>PaymentProcessor</code> interface + factory/registry</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Notifications on events</td>\n<td>Observer / listener interface</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Persist to a DB</td>\n<td>Repository interface with an in-memory implementation</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">interface</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> PricingStrategy</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { Money </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">fee</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(Duration </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">d</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, VehicleType </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">t</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">); }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">class</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> HourlyPricing</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> implements</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> PricingStrategy</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { ... }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">class</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> WeekendPricing</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> implements</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> PricingStrategy</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { ... }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">class</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> ParkingLot</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    private</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> final</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> PricingStrategy pricing;      </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// injected, swappable</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">    ParkingLot</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(PricingStrategy </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">pricing</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">this</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.pricing </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> pricing; }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 488.8 130\" width=\"488.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One interface = one place to extend\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 65 L164 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 65 L164 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M296 65 L352 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M296 65 L352 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M296 65 L352 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M296 65 L352 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ParkingLot</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"43\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">PricingStrategy</text><rect x=\"352\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"414.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">HourlyPricing</text><rect x=\"352\" y=\"74\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"414.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">WeekendPricing</text></svg><figcaption>One interface = one place to extend</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Warning: do not build every seam up front. Add seams for the 2 or 3 most likely changes (which the clarifying questions revealed); for the rest, say how you would refactor.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Interviewer: \"add EV charging spots\". Answer: add <code>EV</code> to <code>SpotType</code>, add <code>ChargingSpot</code> carrying charger state, update the spot-selection strategy; <code>Ticket</code>, <code>PricingStrategy</code>, <code>Level</code> stay unchanged. Three edits, no rewrite.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Plugin systems (IntelliJ, VS Code), Spring's strategy beans, Android <code>RecyclerView.Adapter</code> view types are all seams chosen for known variation.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Wall sockets: any new appliance fits without rewiring the house.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Answering \"I would rewrite it\" or \"just add an <code>if</code>\".</li>\n<li>Interfaces for everything; show seams only where change is plausible.</li>\n<li>Extending by inheritance when composition (strategy) is cleaner.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-interviewers-score","title":"What interviewers score","html":"<p><strong>A typical rubric has 5 to 6 rows, each rated strong / ok / weak.</strong> Know it and aim at every row.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Dimension</th>\n<th>Strong looks like</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Requirements</td>\n<td>Asked focused questions, wrote scope, noted out-of-scope</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Modeling</td>\n<td>Clear entities, right owners of behavior, no god class</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Principles and patterns</td>\n<td>SOLID applied with reason; patterns only where something varies</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Code quality</td>\n<td>Compiles, readable, small methods, validation, meaningful names</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Correctness and edge cases</td>\n<td>Full lot, invalid ticket, double unpark, null inputs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Concurrency</td>\n<td>Named the shared state and protected it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Communication</td>\n<td>Thought aloud, stated trade-offs, took hints well</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 710 68\" width=\"710\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hire signal comes from the combination\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M394 34 L450 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M394 34 L450 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M546 34 L602 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M546 34 L602 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Questions</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Model</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Code</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"498\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Edge cases</text><rect x=\"602\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"650\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Trade-offs</text></svg><figcaption>Hire signal comes from the combination</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Hint handling matters: if the interviewer asks \"what happens if two cars arrive together?\", it is a hint to talk about concurrency. Acknowledge, fix, move on; do not argue.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Candidate A: perfect Strategy + Factory + Observer, but code does not run, no edge cases. Candidate B: simple, correct, runnable, handles full lot and double unpark, explains how to add pricing. B usually wins.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Amazon scores against Leadership Principles (ownership, dive deep) alongside design; Uber/Atlassian machine-coding rounds also score test coverage and code structure.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A driving test: smooth, safe and observant beats flashy.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Optimizing for fancy patterns over correct code.</li>\n<li>Ignoring a hint.</li>\n<li>Not testing your own solution with one worked example (park 3 cars, unpark 1).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"communication-and-recovery","title":"Communication and recovery","html":"<p><strong>Narrate decisions in one sentence each: choice, reason, alternative.</strong> \"I use a <code>Map&#x3C;String, Ticket></code> for lookup by id, O(1); the alternative is scanning a list, O(n).\"</p>\n<p>If you get stuck:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Say what you are stuck on (\"unsure whether the lot or the level owns spot search\").</li>\n<li>Choose one, state the trade-off, continue.</li>\n<li>Offer to revisit at the end.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If you realize a mistake: say it, fix it quickly; interviewers rate recovery highly.</p>\n<p>Do a mini dry run at the end: walk one request through your classes, with real values.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>park(car KA-01) -> Level 0 free car spot #12 -> Ticket T-1 (entry 10:00)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>unpark(T-1) at 12:30 -> 3 hours (rounded up) x Rs 40 = Rs 120</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 643.2 68\" width=\"643.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Stuck? Name it, choose, move on\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 34 L346 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 34 L346 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M485.2 34 L541.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M485.2 34 L541.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Stuck</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Name the choice</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"415.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Pick + trade-off</text><rect x=\"541.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"586.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Continue</text></svg><figcaption>Stuck? Name it, choose, move on</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Google and Meta interview guides repeatedly say \"think out loud\"; mock-interview platforms like Pramp and interviewing.io grade communication as a separate column.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A co-pilot calling out checks so the pilot can trust them.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Long unexplained pauses.</li>\n<li>Defending a flawed choice instead of adjusting.</li>\n<li>Dry running with vague data instead of concrete numbers.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>LLD interviews score: requirements, modeling, principles and patterns, working code, edge cases, concurrency, communication.</li>\n<li>Clarify first (5 to 8 minutes), write scope and out-of-scope, confirm.</li>\n<li>Follow a clock: clarify, entities, diagram, code core, edge cases, extend; have code by minute 18.</li>\n<li>Name by role (nouns for classes, verbs for methods); avoid <code>Manager</code>/<code>Util</code>; one reason to change per class.</li>\n<li>For extensibility, prepare seams for the 2 or 3 likely changes and say exactly what changes when a new one arrives.</li>\n<li>Narrate trade-offs, take hints, dry run with real numbers, and prefer simple correct code over pattern decoration.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}